{"assets":["/statement-assets/e3c2c05877801ec1c8c8152b4cc690466997121f6af3bee886d30cd6e4785667.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"566","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D. Restructuring Company"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Even the most successful company can go through a crisis period when you have to make a hard decision — to restructure, discard and merge departments, fire employees and do other unpleasant stuff. Let's consider the following model of a company."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"There are "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" people working for the Large Software Company. Each person belongs to some "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"department"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". Initially, each person works on his own project in his own department (thus, each company initially consists of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" departments, one person in each)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"However, harsh times have come to the company and the management had to hire a crisis manager who would rebuild the working process in order to boost efficiency. Let's use "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"team(person)"},{"kind":"text","text":" to represent a team where person "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"person"},{"kind":"text","text":" works. A crisis manager can make decisions of two types:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":true},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Merge departments "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"team(x)"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"team(y)"},{"kind":"text","text":" into one large department containing all the employees of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"team(x)"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"team(y)"},{"kind":"text","text":", where "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"y"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ x, y ≤ n"},{"kind":"text","text":") — are numbers of two of some company employees. If "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"team(x)"},{"kind":"text","text":" matches "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"team(y)"},{"kind":"text","text":", then nothing happens. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Merge departments "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"team(x), team(x + 1), ..., team(y)"},{"kind":"text","text":", where "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"y"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ x ≤ y ≤ n"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the numbers of some two employees of the company. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"At that the crisis manager can sometimes wonder whether employees "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"y"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ x, y ≤ n"},{"kind":"text","text":") work at the same department."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Help the crisis manager and answer all of his queries."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of the input contains two integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"q"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ n ≤ 200 000"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ q ≤ 500 000"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the number of the employees of the company and the number of queries the crisis manager has."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Next "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"q"},{"kind":"text","text":" lines contain the queries of the crisis manager. Each query looks like "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"type x y"},{"kind":"text","text":", where "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/e3c2c05877801ec1c8c8152b4cc690466997121f6af3bee886d30cd6e4785667.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":". If "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"type = 1"},{"kind":"text","text":" or "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"type = 2"},{"kind":"text","text":", then the query represents the decision of a crisis manager about merging departments of the first and second types respectively. If "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"type = 3"},{"kind":"text","text":", then your task is to determine whether employees "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"y"},{"kind":"text","text":" work at the same department. Note that "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x"},{"kind":"text","text":" can be equal to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"y"},{"kind":"text","text":" in the query of any type."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each question of type "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"3"},{"kind":"text","text":" print \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"YES"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" or \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"NO"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" (without the quotes), depending on whether the corresponding people work in the same department."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"8 6\n3 2 5\n1 2 5\n3 2 5\n2 4 7\n2 1 2\n3 1 7\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"NO\nYES\nYES\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"D","problemCode":"566D","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/566/problem/D"}